{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 638, "mtime": 1791871062.6929321, "sha256": "38cb51dc0f3f2ef378e7eaf8643b2743bf1ae829466d32cef273ede25fa64c89"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 484, "mtime": 1791871065.913376, "sha256": "5c9072c1d607b123b8c99eca0019d762040e35fb842a83590c64b0f5d1cffe27"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/aa38/omp-938/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/6/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/aa38/omp-938/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/6/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Now a regression test, then I'll run it along with the existing suite.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. I tested this by calling the function directly. pytest isn't installed here, so I haven't run the test files.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, and Python's `round()` rounds that stored value, so it goes down. `round()` also rounds an exact half to the even digit (`0.125` \u2192 `0.12`), which breaks the \"half up\" rule in the docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): turn the float into a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`, which gives the short number you'd type (`\"2.675\"`). Then round to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and convert back to a float, so callers still get the same type.\n\n**Direct calls:** these all came out as expected: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `0.135\u21920.14`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`. `add_vat(10)` still gives `12.0` and `split(10.00, 3)` still gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`.\n\n**Regression test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py` with those same cases. It will run once pytest is installed.\n\n**Remaining issue:** `add_vat` multiplies before rounding (`x * 1.2`), and that multiplication can itself leave a tiny float error. If the product lands just below a half-cent, it will still round down. Fully fixing that means doing the VAT math in `Decimal` as well, which I didn't change.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 250543, "requests_cache_write": 7447, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1304436, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2151, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 8, "score": 1.0, "st